INVALID. 6,606 judgements, ALL graded INCORRECT (0.0% correct) while string
matching on the same rows said 65.8%.

Cause: JUDGE was google/gemini-3.7-flash with max_tokens=5. It is a thinking
model; 5 tokens are consumed by reasoning, so it returned content=null with
finish_reason="length". judge.py then did ("" or "").startswith("CORRECT")
-> False, converting every silent failure into a confident wrong grade.

The previous judge (deepseek-v3.2) was not a thinking model and answered within
5 tokens, so the parameter was fine until the model was swapped.

Fixed in judge.py: max_tokens=2000, and an unparseable verdict now returns None
(ungraded, falls back to string) instead of False.

Kept only as evidence of the failure mode. Do not analyse.
